From ea39fc1eb4cb74035d6fd3f6160799a0de1fedde Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: luxus <7449+luxus@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 5 Aug 2026 16:28:45 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 8/8] fix(nix): put system profile on host service PATH for
 steam
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Dedicated gamescope runs `exec steam -gamepadui …`. The user unit PATH
was only bash/coreutils/pipewire(+gamescope), so steam (programs.steam
→ /run/current-system/sw/bin) was missing: primary child exits, gamescope
dies, no frames. Same class of bug as polaris empty labwc without steam
on PATH. Include config.system.path and common FHS helpers.
---
 packaging/nix/nixos-module.nix | 19 ++++++++++++++++---
 1 file changed, 16 insertions(+), 3 deletions(-)

diff --git a/packaging/nix/nixos-module.nix b/packaging/nix/nixos-module.nix
index d3c758c8..302ef7dd 100644
--- a/packaging/nix/nixos-module.nix
+++ b/packaging/nix/nixos-module.nix
@@ -369,12 +369,25 @@ in
         wantedBy =
           optional cfg.host.autoStart "default.target"
           ++ optional cfg.host.bindToGraphicalSession "graphical-session.target";
-        # The host may exec external helpers (pw-dump, sh, and — for the gamescope/kwin backends —
-        # the compositor). Extend this in your config for a headless gamescope/KWin appliance.
+        # Nested launches (steam, gamescope app, kscreen-doctor, …) resolve via PATH. bash +
+        # coreutils + pipewire alone is NOT enough: a dedicated gamescope does
+        # `exec steam -gamepadui …` and dies with `exec: steam: not found` when steam only lives
+        # under /run/current-system/sw (programs.steam) — same class of bug as polaris empty
+        # labwc when PATH lacked steam. `config.system.path` + common helpers steam's FHS needs.
         path = [
-          pkgs.bash
+          config.system.path
+          pkgs.bashInteractive
           pkgs.coreutils
+          pkgs.findutils
+          pkgs.gnugrep
+          pkgs.gnused
+          pkgs.gawk
+          pkgs.systemd
           pkgs.pipewire
+          pkgs.procps
+          pkgs.util-linux
+          pkgs.which
+          pkgs.bubblewrap
         ]
         # The HDR-capable gamescope, if enabled. On PATH rather than pinned through
         # PUNKTFUNK_GAMESCOPE_BIN so an operator's own override of that env still wins.
